---
import Layout2025 from '../layouts/Layout2025.astro';

const stats = [
  { value: '129', label: 'books read', sub: 'in 2024' },
  { value: '103', label: 'books read', sub: 'in 2025' },
  { value: '8', label: 'friends', sub: 'competing' },
  { value: '2', label: 'languages', sub: 'Spanish + Basque' },
];

const gallery = [
  {
    src: '/case-study/homepage.jpg',
    alt: 'Original homepage with a hero, community intro, and a year-by-year timeline',
    caption: 'The homepage',
  },
  {
    src: '/case-study/year-2026.jpg',
    alt: '2026 competition page showing a top-3 leaderboard of competitors',
    caption: '2026 leaderboard',
  },
  {
    src: '/case-study/competitors-2025.jpg',
    alt: 'Competitors page listing each participant with a short bio, in Basque',
    caption: 'Competitors, in Basque',
  },
  {
    src: '/case-study/books-list-2024.jpg',
    alt: '2024 books grid listing every book read that year with author, tags and points',
    caption: 'Every book of 2024',
  },
  {
    src: '/case-study/books-list-2026.jpg',
    alt: 'The 2026 bookshelf page in Basque, holding a single logged title',
    caption: 'The last shelf, one book in',
  },
  {
    src: '/case-study/book-expanded-synopsis.jpg',
    alt: 'A book card expanded to show its synopsis, tags and the reader who logged it',
    caption: 'A book, expanded',
  },
  {
    src: '/case-study/submit-form.jpg',
    alt: 'Submit a book form gated behind sign-in',
    caption: 'Adding a book',
  },
  {
    src: '/case-study/login.jpg',
    alt: 'Sign in form for the reading club',
    caption: 'Signing in',
  },
  {
    src: '/case-study/team-page.jpg',
    alt: 'Team page with illustrated avatars for each competitor',
    caption: 'The eight of us',
  },
];

const stack = [
  { name: 'Astro', role: 'Static site generation, routing, content collections' },
  { name: 'Vue', role: 'Interactive islands: comments, book feed, submission form' },
  { name: 'Tailwind CSS + daisyUI', role: 'Styling and component primitives' },
  { name: 'Supabase', role: 'Postgres database, authentication, row-level auth' },
  { name: 'Netlify', role: 'Hosting, SSR functions, scheduled rebuilds' },
];

const highlights = [
  {
    title: 'Per-year content collections',
    body: 'Books and competitors were modeled as Astro content collections — one set per year, all validated against two shared Zod schemas. Adding a new reading year meant dropping in a new folder of markdown files.',
    image: '/case-study/books-list-2024.jpg',
    alt: '2024 books grid listing every book read that year with author, tags and points',
  },
  {
    title: 'A friendly points & ranking system',
    body: 'Each book earned points depending on type and length, with a bonus for longer reads. A small calculatePoints() helper did the work, aggregated per competitor to drive the yearly leaderboard.',
    image: '/case-study/year-2026.jpg',
    alt: '2026 competition page showing a top-3 leaderboard of competitors',
  },
  {
    title: 'Auth, submissions & comments',
    body: 'Supabase-managed auth.users plus an app-owned profiles table, linked by a trigger that created a profile on signup, gated the members-only parts. Signed-in readers submitted books and left comments through Vue forms talking to Astro API routes, so the service-role key never reached the browser.',
    image: '/case-study/submit-form.jpg',
    alt: 'Submit a book form gated behind sign-in',
  },
];
---

<Layout2025 title='Irakurketa Lehiaketa — Case Study'>
  <div class='min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-black to-gray-900'>
    <!-- Hero -->
    <header class='relative overflow-hidden min-h-[85vh] flex items-center'>
      <div
        class='absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-basque-10/20 to-basque-20/20 backdrop-blur-3xl'>
      </div>
      <div
        class='relative w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-24 text-center'>
        <p
          class='text-xs md:text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-gray-400 mb-6'>
          Case study · 2024 – 2026 · Retired
        </p>
        <div class='inline-block mb-8 relative'>
          <div
            class='absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-basque-10 to-basque-20 blur-3xl opacity-30'>
          </div>
          <h1
            class='relative text-5xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl font-black text-white tracking-tight'>
            <span
              class='bg-gradient-to-r from-basque-10 via-basque-20 to-basque-10 bg-clip-text text-transparent'>
              Irakurketa Lehiaketa
            </span>
          </h1>
        </div>
        <p class='text-xl md:text-2xl text-gray-300 mb-4 font-light'>
          A reading competition, built as a full-stack side project
        </p>
        <p class='text-base md:text-lg text-gray-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10'>
          Three reading years, two languages, eight friends. The app is gone —
          this is what it looked like, and what building it taught me.
        </p>
        <div class='flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4'>
          <a
            href='#the-site'
            class='inline-flex items-center px-8 py-4 bg-gradient-to-r from-basque-10 to-basque-20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl hover:scale-105 transition-all shadow-lg'>
            See the site that was
          </a>
          <a
            href='#case-study'
            class='inline-flex items-center px-8 py-4 border border-white/20 text-gray-200 font-semibold rounded-xl hover:bg-white/5 hover:border-white/40 transition-all'>
            Read the case study
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a
        href='#the-site'
        aria-label='Scroll to the screenshots'
        class='absolute bottom-8 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-300 transition-colors'>
        <svg
          class='w-6 h-6 animate-bounce'
          fill='none'
          stroke='currentColor'
          stroke-width='1.5'
          viewBox='0 0 24 24'
          aria-hidden='true'>
          <path
            stroke-linecap='round'
            stroke-linejoin='round'
            d='M19.5 8.25 12 15.75 4.5 8.25'></path>
        </svg>
      </a>
    </header>

    <main class='max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 space-y-24'>
      <!-- The site that was -->
      <section id='the-site' class='scroll-mt-20'>
        <p
          class='text-xs md:text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-basque-20 mb-4'>
          In memoriam · 2024 — 2026
        </p>
        <h2 class='text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-6'>
          The site that was
        </h2>
        <p class='text-lg text-gray-300 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-4'>
          For three reading years, eight friends kept score of everything they
          read on a small bilingual site — every page written twice, once in
          Spanish and once in Basque. Books went in, points came out, and each
          December there was a leaderboard to argue about.
        </p>
        <p class='text-lg text-gray-300 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-12'>
          It went offline in 2026. These screenshots, taken the week before it
          was torn down, are all that's left of it.
        </p>

        <div class='grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-16'>
          {
            stats.map(stat => (
              <div class='bg-white/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/10 text-center'>
                <div class='text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black bg-gradient-to-r from-basque-10 to-basque-20 bg-clip-text text-transparent'>
                  {stat.value}
                </div>
                <div class='text-sm font-semibold text-gray-200 mt-2'>
                  {stat.label}
                </div>
                <div class='text-xs text-gray-500'>{stat.sub}</div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>

        <div class='grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4'>
          {
            gallery.map((shot, i) => (
              <a
                href={shot.src}
                target='_blank'
                rel='noopener noreferrer'
                class={`group block ${i === 0 ? 'sm:col-span-2 lg:col-span-3' : ''}`}>
                <div class='overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/10 shadow-xl bg-black/40'>
                  <img
                    src={shot.src}
                    alt={shot.alt}
                    loading='lazy'
                    class={`w-full object-contain object-top transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:scale-[1.02] ${
                      i === 0 ? 'aspect-[16/9]' : 'aspect-[16/10]'
                    }`}
                  />
                </div>
                <p class='mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500 group-hover:text-gray-300 transition-colors'>
                  {shot.caption}
                </p>
              </a>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Case study -->
      <section id='case-study' class='scroll-mt-20'>
        <div
          class='bg-gradient-to-br from-white/10 to-white/5 backdrop-blur-md rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-12 border border-white/20 shadow-2xl'>
          <h2 class='text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-6'>
            How it worked
          </h2>
          <p class='text-lg text-gray-300 leading-relaxed'>
            The brief was modest: more than a shared spreadsheet, less than a
            Goodreads clone. I built it as an Astro site with Vue islands for
            anything interactive, Supabase behind the members-only parts, and
            Netlify running the builds. I maintained it for three seasons, which
            meant living with my own architectural decisions long enough to see
            which ones were wrong.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Tech stack -->
      <section>
        <h2 class='text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-8 text-center'>
          Tech stack
        </h2>
        <div class='grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4'>
          {
            stack.map(item => (
              <div class='bg-white/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/10 hover:border-basque-10/30 transition-all'>
                <h3 class='text-lg font-bold text-white mb-1'>{item.name}</h3>
                <p class='text-sm text-gray-400'>{item.role}</p>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Highlights -->
      <section>
        <h2 class='text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-12 text-center'>
          What I built
        </h2>
        <div class='space-y-16'>
          {
            highlights.map((feature, i) => (
              <div
                class={`grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-center ${
                  i % 2 === 1 ? 'md:[direction:rtl]' : ''
                }`}>
                <div class='md:[direction:ltr]'>
                  <h3 class='text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3'>
                    {feature.title}
                  </h3>
                  <p class='text-gray-300 leading-relaxed'>{feature.body}</p>
                </div>
                <img
                  src={feature.image}
                  alt={feature.alt}
                  class='md:[direction:ltr] rounded-2xl border border-white/10 shadow-xl w-full'
                  loading='lazy'
                />
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Lessons learned -->
      <section>
        <div
          class='bg-gradient-to-br from-white/10 to-white/5 backdrop-blur-md rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-12 border border-white/20 shadow-2xl'>
          <h2 class='text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-6'>
            Lessons learned
          </h2>
          <ul
            class='space-y-4 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed list-disc list-inside'>
            <li>
              Six near-identical collections (one per year, per language) let a
              real bug hide: two of them aliased the same schema objects, and one
              page queried a collection whose folder didn't exist. Astro just
              returned an empty set — no crash, no warning.
            </li>
            <li>
              I'd model it as a single collection with a <code>year</code> field instead
              — same validation, no room for a foldername/collection-name mismatch.
            </li>
            <li>
              Point scoring lived in a client-side JS module. A Postgres view or
              function would have kept it consistent no matter which part of the
              app was asking.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Closing CTA -->
      <section class='text-center'>
        <div
          class='inline-block bg-gradient-to-r from-basque-10 to-basque-20 rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-12 shadow-2xl'>
          <h3 class='text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-4'>
            Want to see the code?
          </h3>
          <p class='text-gray-100 mb-6 max-w-2xl'>
            The full source, including the content collections and Supabase
            integration described above, is on GitHub.
          </p>
          <a
            href='https://github.com/alessandro-giuzio'
            target='_blank'
            rel='noopener noreferrer'
            class='inline-flex items-center px-8 py-4 bg-white text-basque-10 font-bold rounded-xl hover:bg-gray-100 transition-all hover:scale-105 shadow-lg'>
            View on GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>

  <style>
    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }
  </style>
</Layout2025>
